<title>USA: HORSE RACING-HISTORY OF TRIPLE CROWN WINNERS.</title>
<headline>HORSE RACING-HISTORY OF TRIPLE CROWN WINNERS.</headline>
<dateline>ELMONT, New York 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>With a victory</p>
<p>Saturday in the Belmont Stakes, Silver Charm can become the</p>
<p>12th horse in history to win the Triple Crown -- Kentucky</p>
<p>Derby, Preakness Stakes and Belmont Stakes. The following are</p>
<p>the previous Triple Crown winners:</p>
<p> YEAR	HORSE	   JOCKEY		  TRAINER</p>
<p> 1919     Sir Barton    John Loftus	   H.G. Bedwell</p>
<p> 1930     Gallant Fox   Earl Sande	 Sunny Jim Fitzsimmons</p>
<p> 1935     Omaha	   William Saunders Sunny Jim Fitzsimmons</p>
<p> 1937     War Admiral   Charles Kurtsinger  George Conway</p>
<p> 1941     Whirlaway     Eddie Arcaro	  Ben Jones</p>
<p> 1943     Count Fleet   John Longden	  Don Cameron</p>
<p> 1946     Assault	 Warren Mehrtens     Max Hirsch</p>
<p> 1948     Citation	Eddie Arcaro	  Jimmy Jones</p>
<p> 1973     Secretariat   Ron Turcotte	  Lucien Laurin</p>
<p> 1977     Seattle Slew  Jean Cruguet	  Billy Turner</p>
<p> 1978     Affirmed	Steve Cauthen	 Laz Barrera</p>
</text>
